From 50b719183024d676942dbd6f9314f829b57016a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 06:08:33 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] r35 cyclone fix: keep r35.5 guard wording when the
 opponent has no Spell/Trap

The Node Mikanko paired run (r35.5 vs this branch) showed identical moves but
different guard text when the opponent had no S/T at all. The guard now says
"has no opposing Spell/Trap to remove" (r35.5 wording) in that case, and
"has no targetable opposing Spell/Trap" only when their S/T exist but none is
targetable. Moves are unchanged; paired 555/0, 99/0, 99/1 now byte-identical.

optimal-pilot.mjs sha256 e2d9d01d... -> 703f42c18fa5b9be22eddbb732f5a6286e9b6e5498ef398d667c828b84a065d7
Pin proof blocks regenerated; r23-fx re-pinned. SELF-VERIFIED.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HYdavRJmQWYnZCPQsymeGW
